Title: The Tide Ledger
Credit: Table Read narrative-promises fixture (T7.22)
Author: Fixture
Draft date: 2026-07-16

# Planted (never named as a structural label): Nora's promise to return the
# brass compass to Cass resolves by scene 2; Cass's letter to her sister
# never gets sent on the page, so it stays unresolved; Nora's scene-1
# dialogue makes her aim, what she risks, and what stands in her way clear
# without labeling any of it; Cass's "three flashes" line states a hard cap
# on the lighthouse's warning system before consequences follow.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE COTTAGE - NIGHT

NORA turns a tarnished brass compass over in her hands, not looking at Cass.

NORA
Take it back when the tide turns. I'm not keeping what isn't mine.

CASS
You say that every winter, Nora. The tide's always turning.

NORA
(quiet)
Papa asked me to look after this house, not take from it. I need this back in your hands before I can call the debt paid.

CASS
Three flashes, that's the rule. The lamp goes dark on the fourth no matter who's out there — the harbor board doesn't forgive a fourth.

Cass folds a letter she has been writing for weeks and slides it into a drawer, unsealed.

CASS (CONT'D)
(half to herself)
Maybe I'll send this one to my sister. Maybe I won't.

EXT. HARBOR DOCK - DAWN

The tide has turned. NORA presses the brass compass into Cass's palm.

NORA
There. Paid in full. Papa can rest easy, and so can I.

CASS
(surprised, softening)
You didn't have to.

NORA
I did. That's the whole point of a promise.
